# The fuzz crate's own build output and scratch state.
#
# `corpus/` is libFuzzer's working corpus: it grows on every run and is the thing
# the workflow caches between runs, so it must never be committed. `seeds/` is
# the opposite -- the small, reviewed starting corpus that IS committed, and the
# reason it lives elsewhere is so a fuzzing run cannot leave this repo dirty.
target/
corpus/
artifacts/
coverage/
